GCC @gcc@ and Binutils @binutils@ for mipsel-ecoff
==============================================

A cross toolchain for little-endian MIPS with ECOFF objects. The programs
are static, for any Linux on this archive's CPU, with nothing else to
install.

@about@
Unpack it anywhere and put its bin directory on PATH:

    tar xzf @name@-x86_64-linux.tar.gz
    export PATH=$PWD/@name@/bin:$PATH
    mipsel-ecoff-gcc -O2 -msoft-float -c hello.c

Each compiler driver in bin is a small script that points the compiler
at the directory it was unpacked in, so the directory can move, and the
commands can be linked to from elsewhere. Everything else in bin is the
program itself.

There is no C library: link with -nostdlib and your own startup code and
link script, or with the C library or SDK of the system you are
targeting. libgcc is included, with multilibs for @multilibs@.

It is built from the original GNU sources, with a few patches, by
https://github.com/ChrisRx/yaroze-toolchain, which has the sources, the
patches and how to build the same archive with Nix. GCC and Binutils are
free software under the GNU General Public License, in COPYING, and
libgcc's sources add an exception for programs linked with it. The
programs are linked with libiberty and TinyCC's runtime, under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, in COPYING.LIB, and with musl, under the
MIT license, in COPYRIGHT.musl.
